                                                "sense_id": "4be36f67-fcc4-3710-92be-9480576731a9",
                                                "text": "An. The Duke cannot deny the courſe of law: / for the commoditie that ſtrangers haue / With vs in Venice, if it be denied, / Will much impeach the iuſtice of the State, / Since that the trade and profit of the citty / Conſiſteth of all Nations."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0986b754-32d3-4260-bda1-25b1bdc4e225",
                                                "sense_id": "4be36f67-fcc4-3710-92be-9480576731a9",
                                                "text": "As I indicated at the outset, for us Shakespeare's Venetian plays lie between the early modern republic described in Chapter 2, and all the subsequent Venices of our experience, education and imagination, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
